<title>UK: Rio Tinto hits record on strong copper price.</title>
<headline>Rio Tinto hits record on strong copper price.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in mining group Rio Tinto Plc reached a record high on Tuesday as the strength of copper prices continued to boost the stock, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is still powering ahead on the copper price performance,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Rio shares were up 20p at 11.29 stg by 0958 GMT, after earlier reaching a record 11.30 stg. Volume was modest at 676,977 shares.</p>
<p>The stock last week broke through its previous record peak of 10.95 stg, set on June 12, and has risen 8.6 percent in the past eight sessions.</p>
<p>Copper reached $2,602 a tonne in pre-market trading on the London Metal Exchange.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
